<title>LEBANON: Bank of Beirut 1996 profits up.</title>
<headline>Bank of Beirut 1996 profits up.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Beirut and the Arab countries posted a 13.2 percent rise in net profit in 1996, according to its balance sheet published in Beirut newspapers.</p>
<p>Assets climbed by 19.45 percent, customer deposits rose 23.25 percent and loans and credits increased 14.52 percent.</p>
<p>The bank has 26 branches in Lebanon and one abroad. It employs 526 people according to the 1996-1997 almanac of the Lebanese Banks Association.</p>
<p>Results are in billions of Lebanese pounds.</p>
<p>				 1996			 1995</p>
<p> Net profit		 12.85			11.35</p>
<p> Assets		 1,213.619		  1,015.956</p>
<p> Deposits	     1,036.570		    841.023</p>
<p>Loans &amp;</p>
<p> advances		 264.587		    231.029</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 745307 745308 602057</p>
</text>
